# Overrides for the generated documents the dashboard lists and serves.
#
# Copy this file to <config>/project-dashboard/documents.conf and edit it
# (<config> is $SYSTEM_TOOLS_CONFIG, default ~/.config/system); the lines below
# are examples. Without a documents.conf the dashboard lists every found root
# under its directory name and serves nothing outside REPO_ROOT.
#
# This file is no longer the inventory. Any checkout under REPO_ROOT (default
# ~/repos, one group deep at most) that holds `docs/dashboard` is a document
# root, found on disk. Onboarding a repository is a directory in it, not a
# line here, so this list cannot drift behind the fleet.
#
# What a directory cannot say, this file still says. Pipe-separated, because a
# path can hold a space and `read -r a b` splits it in the wrong place.
#
#   label|<key>|<label>              a found root, better named
#   skip|<key>                       a found root the dashboard should not list
#   skip|<key>|<file>                one file of a root, neither listed nor served
#   root|<key>|<label>|<directory>   a root that is somewhere else entirely
#
# Reach for `label|` first. The derived label is the directory name and reads
# badly for an abbreviation -- `mcp-research` becomes `Mcp Research`, and no
# amount of code recovers `MCP` from it -- but that is a naming complaint and
# nothing more, so the line says the name and stops.
#
# `root|` is for a root that genuinely lives elsewhere, and it wins over a
# found root of the same key. Do not use it to rename one: repeating the path
# enumeration already found puts the default location back into this file,
# where it goes stale the moment the repository moves while still looking
# authoritative. That is the drift the enumeration was written to remove.
#
# Two checkouts of the same name in different groups claim one key, and a key
# with two owners has no owner: neither is served, the page names the contest,
# and a `root|` or `skip|` line settles it.
#
# `key` appears in the URL, so it is short and lowercase. The directory is
# read, never written, and only its regular `.html` files are ever served.

# An abbreviation the derived label would spell `Mcp Research`.
label|mcp-research|MCP

# A found root that should not be listed.
skip|scratch-notes

# One stale page of a root that stays listed. The file is its name in the root.
skip|mcp-research|old-survey.html

# A vault is not a checkout under ~/repos, so nothing finds it; a root| line
# is the only way its docs/dashboard is served. `~` and spaces both survive.
root|vault|Vault|~/Documents/My Vault/docs/dashboard
